{
    "marked": false,
    "answer": "<p>The <b>Direct each site to upload data into an S3 bucket in the nearest AWS Region. Then use S3 Cross-Region Replication to transfer data to the central S3 bucket. After replication, delete the data from the original S3 bucket.<\/b> option is the best solution. This approach leverages local buckets to minimize latency during upload and allows AWS to automatically handle replication, significantly reducing operational overhead and ensuring data is aggregated quickly.<br><br> The <i>Use Amazon EC2 instances in the closest Region for each site...<\/i> option is more complex, as it adds unnecessary steps (using EC2, EBS snapshots/restores), driving up both cost and management overhead compared to simple S3-to-S3 transfers.<br><br> The <i>Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the target S3 bucket...<\/i> option, while accelerating uploads, doesn't aggregate or reconcile data from multiple regions and is generally less optimal for very large daily data volumes across global locations.<br><br> The <i>Schedule daily AWS Snowball Edge jobs for each location...<\/i> method is well-suited for offline data migration or where internet bandwidth is limited, but in this case each site already has a high-speed connection, so using Snowball is operationally unnecessary and adds delay.<br><br><b>Tips:<\/b> S3 Cross-Region Replication automates data movement between buckets across regions, helping simplify management of global datasets. For large-scale, frequent uploads from multiple geographies, always try to use AWS services (like S3 CRR) that reduce operational burden and ensure consistency.<br><\/p>",
    "query": "<p>A company gathers temperature, humidity, and pressure readings from cities located around the world. Each site generates approximately 500 GB of data daily, and all sites have high-speed Internet connections. The company\u2019s goal is to quickly consolidate all the global data into a single Amazon S3 bucket, while minimizing operational overhead. <br><br> Which approach best fulfills these needs?<\/p>",
