    "id": 12,
    "query": "A financial services company is migrating its internal infrastructure to AWS from an on-premises data center. Due to strict data residency regulations, the company must operate exclusively in the <strong>Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region (ap-northeast-3)</strong>. Additionally, security policies prohibit any VPCs from having internet access. What are the most appropriate AWS-native solutions to enforce these regional and network restrictions while maintaining centralized governance?",
    "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answers: Option 1 and Option 2</strong></p><p><strong>Option 1:</strong> AWS Organizations with SCPs can enforce governance rules across accounts. You can block all Regions except ap-northeast-3 and prevent VPCs from creating internet gateways, thereby enforcing data residency and network isolation policies at scale.</p><p><strong>Option 2:</strong> AWS Config provides visibility into noncompliant resources through managed rules that monitor VPC internet gateway usage and deployment in unauthorized Regions. Though it doesn't prevent violations, it ensures real-time alerts and auditability.</p><p><strong>Why other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Option 3:</strong> AWS Control Tower is not available in ap-northeast-3.</li><li><strong>Option 4:</strong> AWS WAF is not designed for outbound traffic control and cannot enforce Region restrictions.</li><li><strong>Option 5:</strong> Network ACLs are limited in scope and IAM policies cannot restrict Region usage.</li></ul><p><strong>Why this question is challenging:</strong> It tests your understanding of both proactive (SCP) and reactive (Config) compliance strategies, and requires awareness of service availability by Region.</p>",
    "marked": 0,
    "timespent": 0,
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "Use AWS Organizations to define service control policies (SCPs) that block access to all Regions except ap-northeast-3 and prevent VPCs from attaching internet gateways.",
        "correct": true,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Use AWS Config to enable managed rules that detect internet gateways and monitor for resources deployed outside the ap-northeast-3 Region. Configure alerts for noncompliance.",
        "correct": true,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Use AWS Control Tower to set up landing zones with guardrails that deny internet access and restrict Region usage to ap-northeast-3.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Use AWS WAF to block outbound internet traffic and configure account settings to disable access to all Regions except ap-northeast-3.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Create network ACLs that deny traffic to and from 0.0.0.0/0. Assign IAM policies to users that restrict access to all Regions except ap-northeast-3.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      }
