    "id": 14,
    "query": "A digital audio platform sells custom ringtones created from snippets of trending music. These ringtone files are stored in <strong>Amazon S3 Standard</strong> and are each at least 256 KB in size. The platform hosts millions of these files, but downloads are uncommon for any ringtone that is more than 120 days old. The company wants to reduce its storage costs while keeping frequently accessed ringtones immediately available to users. What is the <strong>MOST cost-effective</strong> way to meet these requirements?",
    "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answer: Option 1</strong></p><p>Implementing an S3 Lifecycle policy that transitions files from S3 Standard to S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 120 days helps optimize cost without sacrificing availability for newer or frequently downloaded files. Because the ringtone files are at least 256 KB in size, they meet the minimum size requirement for transition to S3 Standard-IA, which is more cost-effective for infrequently accessed data.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Option 2:</strong> Intelligent-Tiering adds per-object monitoring charges, which are unnecessary for a predictable access pattern.</li><li><strong>Option 3:</strong> Manual management with S3 Inventory is inefficient and does not scale well.</li><li><strong>Option 4:</strong> S3 Standard-IA is not suited for frequently accessed newly uploaded data and incurs retrieval charges and minimum storage durations.</li></ul><p><strong>Why this question is challenging:</strong> It tests your ability to match predictable storage patterns with lifecycle transitions and understand storage tier cost tradeoffs.</p>",
    "marked": 0,
    "timespent": 0,
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "Implement an S3 Lifecycle policy that moves the objects from S3 Standard to S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 120 days.",
        "correct": true,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Use S3 Intelligent-Tiering and configure it to move files to a lower-cost access tier automatically after 120 days of inactivity.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Configure the S3 inventory feature to manage and manually transition files to S3 Standard-IA after 120 days.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Use S3 Standard-IA as the initial storage class when uploading ringtone files to immediately benefit from lower storage costs.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      }
    ],
    "objectives": []
