    "id": 15,
    "query": "A pharmaceutical research lab is storing sensitive clinical trial results in an Amazon S3 bucket. A small group of researchers must be able to upload new data, while the rest of the team should have read-only access. No one, including administrators, should be allowed to edit or delete existing data. Additionally, each file must be retained for at least 1 year after it is uploaded, to comply with regulatory standards. What is the best way to meet these requirements?",
    "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answer: Option 1</strong></p><p>S3 Object Lock in compliance mode with a 365-day retention period enforces WORM (Write Once, Read Many) protection. This ensures that no user, including administrators, can modify or delete an object during the retention period. This configuration fully satisfies the regulatory requirement to prevent changes and deletions for at least one year.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Option 2:</strong> Governance mode allows overrides by privileged users, which violates the requirement.</li><li><strong>Option 3:</strong> IAM and bucket policies can be changed by admins and do not provide immutable retention.</li><li><strong>Option 4:</strong> Monitoring via Lambda and checksums adds complexity but does not enforce protection against deletion or overwrite.</li></ul><p><strong>Why this question is challenging:</strong> It tests your ability to differentiate between access control and immutable storage in regulated environments.</p>",
    "marked": 0,
    "timespent": 0,
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "Enable S3 Object Lock in compliance mode and set a retention period of 365 days for each object.",
        "correct": true,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Enable S3 Object Lock in governance mode and apply a legal hold of 1 year on each object.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Create an IAM role that blocks delete and overwrite actions for all users. Use a bucket policy to allow only that role to interact with the S3 bucket.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Configure the S3 bucket to trigger an AWS Lambda function upon object creation. Have the function store and verify the object\u2019s checksum to detect any modifications.",
        "correct": false,
        "selected": false
      }
    ],
