    "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answer: Amazon CloudFront</strong></p><p>Amazon CloudFront is AWS\u2019s CDN that delivers both live and on-demand streaming content from edge locations worldwide. It integrates with AWS Media Services and supports protocols like HLS, improving playback performance globally. It caches on-demand videos and delivers live content with low latency.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Option 2:</strong> Global Accelerator does not cache or optimize video content for streaming.</li><li><strong>Option 3:</strong> Route 53 is a DNS service and does not deliver or cache video streams.</li><li><strong>Option 4:</strong> S3 Transfer Acceleration is for speeding up uploads to S3, not streaming playback.</li></ul>",
