    "query": "An online retail business runs its analytics workload in the AWS Cloud. The application generates approximately 500 MB of JSON data every month. For disaster recovery purposes, the company needs to back up this data. Backups must be retained for 45 days and must be accessible within milliseconds if recovery is required. Which is the most cost-effective solution that meets these requirements?",
    "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answer: Amazon S3 Standard</strong></p><p>Amazon S3 Standard provides immediate, millisecond access to stored objects, and is ideal for data that must be quickly retrievable. For 500 MB/month and 45-day retention, the cost remains low and avoids the complexity and retrieval delays of colder storage tiers.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Option 2:</strong> S3 Glacier has long retrieval times, which does not meet the millisecond access requirement.</li><li><strong>Option 3:</strong> RDS is for relational databases and would unnecessarily complicate backup storage for static JSON files.</li><li><strong>Option 4:</strong> OpenSearch is meant for analytics and search, not as a backup solution with rapid access needs.</li></ul>",
