    "query": "A digital media company operates a backend application on Amazon EC2 that processes incoming messages from an Amazon SQS queue. The workload is bursty and unpredictable\u2014some hours may have thousands of messages, while others may have none. The application is designed for high availability and must continue processing messages with minimal cost and no downtime. What is the most cost-effective and reliable compute strategy for this scenario?",
    "answer": "Deploy a mix of EC2 Reserved Instances for steady-state traffic and Spot Instances to dynamically scale during message surges.<br><br>This approach balances reliability with cost efficiency. Reserved Instances provide guaranteed capacity for the baseline level of processing and reduce long-term costs. Spot Instances allow the application to scale out at a much lower cost when message volume increases, and since SQS decouples the producer and consumer, occasional interruption of Spot Instances won\u2019t result in message loss.",
