{
  "id": 2,
  "query": "<p>A financial services company is migrating its core accounting platform to AWS. The platform runs on a Windows environment and needs access to a shared file system that can be simultaneously mounted by multiple Amazon EC2 Windows servers located in different Availability Zones. What is the most appropriate AWS service or configuration to fulfill this requirement?</p>",
  "answer": "<p>The correct answer is: <strong>Use Amazon FSx for Windows File Server and mount the FSx file share on each EC2 Windows instance.</strong></p><p>Amazon FSx for Windows File Server provides a fully managed, scalable, and highly available shared file system built on Windows Server. It supports the SMB protocol, making it the ideal choice for Windows applications that require a shared file system across multiple instances—even across different Availability Zones within the same region. FSx also integrates with Microsoft Active Directory for authentication and access control.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><p><strong>Using AWS Storage Gateway in volume gateway mode</strong> is not suitable in this context. Volume gateway mode creates iSCSI block volumes, not SMB-compatible shared file systems. It is typically used for hybrid scenarios between on-premises environments and AWS, not for sharing files across EC2 Windows instances.</p><p><strong>Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)</strong> is designed for Linux-based workloads and supports the NFS protocol, which is not natively compatible with Windows-based applications. It does not support Windows authentication methods like Active Directory or SMB shares.</p><p><strong>Amazon EBS volumes</strong> are block-level storage devices that can only be attached to one EC2 instance at a time in a given Availability Zone. They do not support simultaneous access by multiple EC2 instances and are not designed to function as shared file systems.</p><p><strong>Why this question matters:</strong> This question tests a candidate's understanding of the right AWS file storage service for Windows workloads, especially when high availability and multi-AZ deployment are involved. Many candidates incorrectly assume that EFS or EBS will work for Windows, so it’s important to remember FSx is the only native Windows file system offering in AWS with full SMB support.</p><p><strong>Tip:</strong> When the question specifies <em>Windows</em> and <em>shared file system</em> with <em>multi-AZ</em> access, look immediately to FSx for Windows File Server. Don’t be distracted by Linux-centric or hybrid storage solutions like EFS or Storage Gateway.</p>",
  "marked": 0,
  "timespent": 0,
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Deploy Amazon FSx for Windows File Server and connect each EC2 instance to the shared file system using SMB.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Set up AWS Storage Gateway in volume gateway mode and mount the resulting iSCSI volume to all EC2 Windows instances.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
