      "text": "Build an Amazon Pinpoint journey and configure it to forward events to an Amazon Kinesis data stream for analysis and long-term storage.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) to send SMS messages and trigger a Lambda function for processing incoming replies.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Create an Amazon SNS FIFO topic and subscribe a Kinesis data stream to collect responses for processing and archiving.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    }
  ],
  "objectives": []
},
{
  "id": "201a",
  "query": "<p>A company currently uses Amazon Pinpoint for sending campaigns, managing segments, and tracking analytics. The company wants to ensure continuity as Amazon Pinpoint phases out support. Which AWS service should the company use to migrate its engagement features?</p>",
  "answer": "<p>The correct answer is: <strong>Amazon Connect proactive engagement features such as outbound campaigns and Customer Profiles.</strong></p><p>Amazon Pinpoint engagement features (segments, campaigns, journeys, and analytics) will be deprecated by <strong>October 30, 2026</strong>. Customers using these capabilities are advised to migrate to <strong>Amazon Connect’s proactive engagement suite</strong>, which supports similar features like outbound messaging, unified analytics, and Customer Profiles that consolidate contact points into a single record. These features allow for continued customer communication across multiple channels with integrated reporting.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><p><strong>Amazon SES</strong> is suitable for email sending and will offer email deliverability dashboards, but it does not replace campaigns or segment management.</p><p><strong>Amazon Kinesis</strong> is used for event streaming and analytics but does not replace customer engagement workflows like campaigns or journeys.</p><p><strong>AWS End User Messaging</strong> is the rebranded messaging API layer for SMS and related protocols, but it does not offer segmentation or analytics tooling for engagement strategies.</p>",
