{
  "id": "201b",
  "query": "<p>A company uses Amazon Pinpoint to send two-way SMS and push notifications through APIs. The company recently learned that Amazon Pinpoint will stop accepting new customers in 2025. What is the best course of action for continuing to use messaging channel APIs beyond 2026?</p>",
  "answer": "<p>The correct answer is: <strong>Continue using the rebranded APIs now offered under AWS End User Messaging, which will remain supported after Amazon Pinpoint is deprecated.</strong></p><p>Amazon Pinpoint’s messaging APIs for SMS, MMS, push, WhatsApp, and voice have been rebranded as <strong>AWS End User Messaging</strong> as of Q3 2024. These APIs will remain fully supported and are not affected by the 2026 deprecation of Amazon Pinpoint’s engagement features. Existing applications can continue to use these messaging APIs without service interruption or major changes.</p><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><p><strong>Amazon Connect</strong> is primarily used for proactive engagement and contact center functionality. While it supports some messaging workflows, it does not replace direct SMS or push API usage.</p><p><strong>Amazon SES</strong> supports email but does not handle SMS, push, or voice messaging use cases.</p><p><strong>Amazon Kinesis</strong> is used for stream processing and analytics, not direct message delivery.</p>",
