{
  "id": 234,
  "query": "<p>A company is developing a new web-based customer relationship management (CRM) application. The application will run on Amazon EC2 instances with Amazon EBS volumes behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB), and will use an Amazon Aurora database. The company requires that <strong>all data</strong> be encrypted <strong>at rest</strong> and <strong>in transit</strong>.</p><p>Which solution will meet these requirements? (Choose 1)</p>",
  "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answer:</strong><br><strong>Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to encrypt the EBS volumes and Aurora database storage at rest. Attach an AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) certificate to the ALB to encrypt data in transit.</strong></p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong><br>This solution uses AWS-native tools that are purpose-built for encryption:</p><ul><li><strong>AWS KMS</strong> enables encryption of EBS volumes and Amazon Aurora storage using customer managed or AWS-managed keys, fulfilling the requirement for encryption at rest.</li><li><strong>AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)</strong> provides and manages SSL/TLS certificates that can be used with ALBs to encrypt data in transit.</li></ul><p><strong>Why the other options are incorrect:</strong></p><ul><li><em>Using AWS KMS certificates on the ALB</em>: AWS KMS does not provide SSL/TLS certificates for ALBs. ACM is the correct service for in-transit encryption with ALBs.</li><li><em>Using the root account to enable encryption account-wide</em>: AWS does not offer a global setting to enable encryption for all services with a single switch. Root usage is discouraged.</li><li><em>Using BitLocker and importing TLS keys to KMS</em>: BitLocker is not an AWS-native solution and cannot be applied to EC2/EBS in this way. TLS certificates should be managed with ACM, not KMS.</li></ul>",
  "marked": 0,
  "timespent": 0,
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) certificates on the ALB to encrypt data in transit. Use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to encrypt the EBS volumes and Aurora database storage at rest.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use the AWS root account to log in to the AWS Management Console. Upload the company’s encryption certificates. While in the root account, select the option to turn on encryption for all data at rest and in transit for the account.",
